<BaseLayout title="Terms of Use – Gamepad Tester" description="Terms of use for Gamepad Tester: free browser tools provided as-is, local input processing, no hardware warranty, trademarks and advertising.">
  <section class="article-hero"><div class="shell article-hero-inner"><span class="subpage-kicker">TERMS OF USE</span><h1>Free tools.<br /><span>Plain terms.</span></h1><p class="lede">These terms apply to every page on checkgamepad.com. By using the site you agree to them. Effective date: November 7, 2026.</p></div></section>
  <section class="subpage-content shell">
    <article class="info-card"><span class="panel-label">01 / THE SERVICE</span><h2>Tools provided as-is</h2><p>Gamepad Tester offers free browser-based tests for controllers, keyboards and mice. The tools are provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy or uninterrupted availability.</p><p>We may change, add or remove tools and pages at any time without notice.</p></article>
    <article class="info-card"><span class="panel-label">02 / LOCAL PROCESSING</span><h2>Runs in your browser</h2><p>The tests run locally in your browser. Controller, keyboard and mouse input is read through standard browser APIs to draw the result on screen and is not uploaded to us. The optional vibration test only asks your browser to play a rumble effect through drivers your operating system already loaded.</p><p>The <a class="inline-link" href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> describes what data the site and its service providers do handle.</p></article>
    <article class="info-card"><span class="panel-label">03 / NO HARDWARE DIAGNOSIS</span><h2>Readings are not a repair verdict</h2><p>Results show the signals your browser exposes, which depend on the browser, operating system, connection type, driver and controller mode. A reading on this site is not a professional hardware diagnosis and is no warranty that a device is faulty or healthy.</p><p>Do not rely on it alone when deciding to repair, return, buy or sell a device. You use the tools at your own risk, and to the extent permitted by law we are not liable for any loss or damage arising from their use.</p></article>
    <article class="info-card"><span class="panel-label">04 / TRADEMARKS</span><h2>No affiliation</h2><p>PlayStation and DualSense are trademarks of Sony Interactive Entertainment. Xbox is a trademark of Microsoft. Nintendo Switch and Joy-Con are trademarks of Nintendo. The 8BitDo and Logitech names belong to their respective owners, as do all other product names mentioned on the site.</p><p>They are used only to describe compatibility. Gamepad Tester is independent and is not affiliated with, sponsored or endorsed by any of these companies.</p></article>
    <article class="info-card"><span class="panel-label">05 / ADS AND THIRD PARTIES</span><h2>Advertising and outside content</h2><p>The site may show advertising and uses third-party services such as analytics. Ads and linked third-party sites are provided by others; we do not control their content and are not responsible for their products, services or privacy practices.</p></article>
    <article class="info-card"><span class="panel-label">06 / ACCEPTABLE USE</span><h2>Using the site fairly</h2><p>Use the site for personal diagnostics. Do not attempt to disrupt it, overload it with automated requests, or copy its pages and code for redistribution as your own service.</p></article>
    <article class="info-card"><span class="panel-label">07 / CHANGES</span><h2>Updates to these terms</h2><p>We may update these terms when the site changes. The effective date at the top of this page shows when they were last revised, and continued use after a change means you accept the updated terms.</p></article>
    <article class="info-card"><span class="panel-label">08 / CONTACT</span><h2>Questions</h2><p>Questions about these terms can be sent to <a class="inline-link" href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a> or through the <a class="inline-link" href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p></article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
